From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] unit: test one HFP emulator serving the calls of two modems

Build the emulator, voicecall, GAtServer and D-Bus helpers into a test,
with a small model of the modem and atom layer (atoms prepended,
watches told before an atom's unregister runs, a modem going away
unregistering and freeing its atoms in list order), a ready SIM and a
scripted voicecall driver on each of two modems. The headset is the
other end of a socketpair and sets up the service level connection with
AT+BRSF, AT+CIND, AT+CMER and AT+CLIP.

It checks that:
- a call ringing on the second modem gives the headset +CIEV callsetup,
  RING and +CLIP with its number;
- ATA and AT+CHUP for that call reach the second modem's driver, and
  AT+CLCC lists the call;
- the same works for a call on the first modem;
- a call that comes and goes on one modem, or that modem going away,
  does not end the headset's view of an active call on the other;
- ATD dials on the first modem when idle, and on the modem that has a
  call when one exists;
- the first modem going away leaves the second one answering;
- a handler only one modem has is freed when that modem goes, and its
  command then answers ERROR;
- a modem added to a live link is served;
- AT+BAC is accepted with CVSD second and rejected without CVSD.

voicecall registers a D-Bus interface, so the test needs a bus; like
test-hfp-ag-bluez5 it skips itself without one. The asserts stay on in
a build with NDEBUG.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

